      "role": "user",
      "content": "okay, glad to hear it's not actual creatures lol. i was a bit thrown off there. \n\nbut back to the technical side—if it's just the wood settling, how do i differentiate between \"normal settling\" and actual structural failure? like, if i see a crack in a beam or a gap in a joint that's getting wider, is there a specific threshold or measurement i should be looking for to know it's more than just the fir \"breathing\"? i don't want to ignore something that's actually dangerous.",
